{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S51-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"222a4f9275bb05e9263838ac916ed34033cb9a2482b49f34fc42e62a4a85bcd3\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 requires rind identification for panel membership; A5 extends that qualification requirement to questions.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 rejects B2's eating motive as a qualification; A5 answers B4's request to ask why, although abstractly.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 wants cheese rather than membership; B4's generic question supplies little additional pressure.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 adds questions to the admission restriction but leaves the original rind test unchanged.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a cheese panel and an identifiable rind; B2 makes B's immediate appetite playable.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Consumption is not qualification' is economical; A5's 'Questions shape the panel' is more explanatory.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 80\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Before joining our cheese panel, identify this rind.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I just came to eat cheese.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Then identify it for the tasting queue. Judging requires the county certificate.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I have that certificate. I teach the county course.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Wonderful. Before you examine our cheese, let me examine your syllabus.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses subject expertise and qualifying standards to control participation, then subjects an apparent expert to a further standard.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Arbitrary obstruction or private veto.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 names a rind-identification test; revised A3 and A5 make access depend on credentials and curriculum rather than A's unexplained consent.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a now tests a visitor whose expertise exceeds expectations; b defensively credentializes a challenge to the gatekeeper's own authority.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original B4 gave A5 little new material. The revision preserves the cheese-panel setting and makes B4's teaching credential cause A5's syllabus inspection. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. A1/A3 establish standards, B2/B4 change eligibility, and A5 expands scrutiny coherently. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 can sound knowingly evasive unless A sincerely believes inspecting the syllabus protects standards.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S51-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"7c33169864c357b5b11af3adab1c98e15ce5272b6684aca5e12270b178631954\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 conditions judging on a pruning certificate; A5 requires advanced qualification even to question A.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 lowers the certificate level in response to B2's street scale; A5 gates B4's certification challenge.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 contests excessive requirements and B4 turns the credential test back on its administrator.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 extends expertise policing from judging gardens to examining the examiner's authority.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes garden judging and pruning credentials; B2 specifies a modest street competition.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's 'street-level certificate' and A5's 'advanced certificate' efficiently develop the same qualification ladder.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"You may judge the garden competition once I check your pruning certificate.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I'm filling in for my wife. She's broken her ankle.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Then show me where you'd cut this rose. We can assess you here.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"She could judge by video. I'll carry the phone.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Good. First demonstrate that you can distinguish a diseased leaf from a blurry one.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes participation depend on demonstrated competence, extending qualification checks to the supporting role in B's proposed solution.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Arbitrary obstruction or private veto.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 offers an actual pruning assessment after B2 explains the substitution; A5 tests whether B's video work can support reliable judging rather than withholding unexplained consent.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a audits an unexpectedly expert visitor's syllabus; b accommodates an injured judge while qualifying the replacement's new camera role. The frozen a record retains its earlier comparison as required.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The rejected candidate repeated invented certificate levels and gave B little practical purpose. The revision keeps garden judging and adds an injured spouse and remote-judging solution. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, because A1/A3/A5 condition each role on relevant competence; logic 5, because B2 prompts an on-site assessment and B4 prompts a camera assessment; relationship 4, because B2 seeks to cover for a spouse and B4 offers a workable alternative; heightening 4, because A5 extends scrutiny to the helper; specificity 5, because A1's competition and A3's rose establish playable work; brevity/wit 4, because A5's diseased-versus-blurry distinction follows the new role. Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; all dialogue gates pass. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's camera test is a modest extension of legitimate judging standards; the comedy depends on A treating even this supporting role as a formal qualification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S52-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"eaf56b78cf349f970255e6187af321d405601572bad8d3b6da53f35c03d2d969\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 claims 'my own table,' but B2 requests booking rather than proof of a role, and A5 expresses no clear insult.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 distinguishes possession from B2's booking requirement; A5 responds to B4's occupants, though 'borrowing my problem' is unclear.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 enforces a universal booking rule and B4 reports occupancy, but neither clarifies A's relationship to the venue.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 maintains ownership language without specifying what the occupants must now do.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 gives a waiting list and table but leaves whether A is owner, regular customer or host unresolved.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's 'People seeking a table book' is concise; A5's borrowing metaphor obscures the practical move.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 66\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Why is someone sitting in my chair at the founders' dinner?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"He's a sponsor. Have you brought your founder's invitation?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"You need an envelope to establish that I founded this place?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I know you did. I'll bring another chair.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"For him, thank you. Put mine back at the head.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A assumes the founder's place already belongs to them and treats documentary verification as an affront.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General entitlement to preferential service.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A1 identifies the founder's place, A3 takes offense at the invitation requirement, and A5 accepts help only on terms preserving that place.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a asserts an established founder's status and redirects a helpful accommodation; b assumes an office before its election and rejects nomination.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original did not clearly establish a role or an insulting proof demand. The new illustrative setting is a founders' dinner. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. B2 supplies the offending invitation test; B4's extra chair causes A5 to assign that chair to the sponsor. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's historical claim is accepted within the fiction; the comic behavior is the inflexible claim to seating precedence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S52-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"162f27bac2e1fed467b8ef62118352f772fa827e4b3044be60a38a643fca57f0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 physically claims the committee chair; A3 assumes legitimacy and A5 explicitly finds nomination insulting.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 recasts B2's election as confirmation; A5 answers B4's nomination requirement with the existing nameplate.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 uphold the committee's selection procedure, forcing A to reinterpret two distinct prerequisites.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 promotes A1's nameplate from a possession marker into sufficient evidence of nomination.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1's nameplate and committee chair make the claim visible through speech; B4 supplies a concrete procedural obstacle.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5's 'The nameplate already has' economically converts the established prop into A's response.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"I've put my nameplate on the allotment committee chair. Let's start.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"Have you got the result sheet? I need to verify who's chairing.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"You want me to prove I'm entitled to my own chair?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I'll call the secretary. She can confirm it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Put her on speaker. Once she's confirmed me, I'll ask her to minute your apology.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A occupies the committee chair as an existing right and treats verification of that role as an offense requiring acknowledgment.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ambition to win leadership.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 begins chairing rather than seeking support; A3 takes the proof request personally, and A5 uses B4's verification call to demand an apology.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a redirects a helpful seating accommodation for an acknowledged founder; b turns a clerk's verification process into public vindication of disputed committee authority. The frozen a record retains its earlier comparison as required.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The rejected candidate substituted nameplate wordplay for development and made the proof demand indirect. The revision specifies an allotment committee, a missing result sheet and a secretary who can verify it. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, because A1 assumes occupancy and A3/A5 treat proof as insulting; logic 5, because B2's verification request causes A3's offense and B4's call supplies A5's public audience and minute-taker; relationship 4, because B2 needs an accurate chairing record and B4 offers a practical check; heightening 4, because A5 demands an official apology; specificity 4, because A1/B2 establish the meeting and missing evidence while leaving the result unresolved; brevity/wit 4, because A5 turns the proposed confirmation into a concrete additional demand. Total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; all dialogue gates pass. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 is more affronted than affectionate. The secretary's actual answer remains open, so the scene does not establish that A's entitlement is valid.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S53-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"8a1b6d40fc9f3e7d9473ca4155243cdf77947988c729c664c76ba3971cdd358f\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 hands over the café key and A3 reclaims approval after B2 changes hours; A5 reduces leadership to resemblance.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2's changed hours prompt A3's consultation rule; B4's reminder prompts A5's reinterpretation of being in charge.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 acts as a successor and B4 invokes A's promise, exposing the tension between handoff and control.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 comments on the successor's appearance of authority rather than taking a further concrete decision back.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1's café key and B2's opening hours establish a playable business handover.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5's 'help you resemble it' is compact, but makes A unusually explicit about undermining the handover.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Here's the café key. Your first day in charge. I'll watch quietly.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I'm opening an hour later. You won't have to come in.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Check timetable changes with me first. Regulars need continuity.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I'll explain it to them myself.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Good practice. I'll stand beside you and handle any questions about the hours.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A prepares a successor to lead but restores personal authority when that successor's independence would make A unnecessary.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary micromanagement.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 explicitly hands over leadership; B2 removes A's need to attend, causing A3's approval requirement and A5's reclaimed public voice.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses protective mentoring to preserve daily relevance; b reasserts the approval machinery threatened by a deputy's first reform.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original A5 described sham authority too openly. The revision preserves the café handover and opening-hours seed. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. B4 offers independent explanation; A5 turns that offer into supervised practice and reserves answers for A. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The final intervention is small in scale, but clearly takes the successor's customer-facing authority back.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S53-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a41a8ef62940e75d8548f0bf0ea53f152da485e8fedcba5f14a11ea85fbef6f3\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 installs the deputy as meeting leader; A3 immediately reclaims approval when B2 threatens the old process.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's proposed removal; A5 recasts B4's explicit correction as a leadership lesson about the predecessor.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 exercises the offered authority and B4 refuses to overlook A's contradiction.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 extends A3's procedural control into the successor's training and treatment of the former chair.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 names the deputy and meeting chair; B2 identifies the exact approval process at stake.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Excellent confidence. I'll need to approve that' compactly joins encouragement to repossession of authority.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Take my chair, deputy. Lead the meeting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"First, staff rotas won't need your approval anymore.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Excellent confidence. I'll need to approve that.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I've already told the staff to send their rotas directly to me.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Then tell them I'll do the final review beside you. You should see how approval works before abolishing it.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A offers a deputy succession, then restores final authority through instruction when the deputy redirects decisions away from A.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A standing superior simply enforcing procedure.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 hands over the chair before B2 removes A's approval role; A5 responds to B4's independent announcement by making the successor announce A's final review.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a reclaims customer-facing authority through protective mentoring; b reclaims institutional review after the deputy has already announced a new reporting route.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The rejected A5 retreated from a sharp approval reversal into a generic lesson about tact. The revision keeps the meeting handoff and makes the approval process concern staff rotas. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, because A1 gives leadership and A3/A5 reclaim it after independence; logic 5, because B2 directly triggers A3 and B4's staff announcement requires A5's corrective announcement; relationship 4, because B2 proposes a reform and B4 has begun implementing it; heightening 4, because A5 restores final review publicly as training; specificity 5, because A1's chair and B2/B4's rota route supply concrete work; brevity/wit 4, because A5 makes abolishing approval require instruction in submitting to it. Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; all dialogue gates pass. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's lesson remains explicit, but it now carries a concrete final-review demand rather than only a reprimand.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S54-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"bd7c020c13fb060a2ca62730f8bb0a657a8e130501595a064ca739b83e6068ae\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 warmly supports the exhibition while withholding the room signature; A5 maintains the pleasant refusal.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's revision question without criteria; A5 reuses B4's 'perfect' assessment to justify delay.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 seeks actionable changes and B4 cites prior approval, but B has no concrete deadline or alternative.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 continues withholding the same signature without adding a fresh consequence or controlling tactic.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies an exhibition and room form, making the practical obstacle immediately clear.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5's 'spoil it with a premature signature' follows the pleasant obstruction, though it mainly restates the premise.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 80\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"I'd love your exhibition to happen. I haven't signed the room form yet.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"The installer needs it by four. Is there anything I can change?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Nothing. It's lovely. I just need to feel ready.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I'll book the other gallery. They don't need your signature.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"I'll gladly introduce you. Let me approve the email before you send it.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A remains accommodating while making progress depend on personal consent, extending that dependency when B finds another route.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Legitimate quality assurance.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 says nothing needs changing, yet withholds consent; A5 claims approval over B's alternative-gallery email.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a follows B's attempt to move the exhibition elsewhere; b absorbs B's offer to help obtain the funding code.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original ended with a restatement. The revised exhibition scene gives B a deadline and alternative venue. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. B4 removes the signature dependency; A5 pleasantly creates an email-approval dependency. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 asserts informal control over an introduction; B remains free to refuse, keeping the scene open.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S54-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"fe1aa451092b305db0a5fd84b6e3b76afbe41b6feeea1123161b2f37ed9384b0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 offers encouragement and A3 withholds consent, but states the distinction more openly than quietly cooperative behavior suggests.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's code request with a consent condition; A5 explains B4's requested distinction through the code's six digits.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 needs access to funds; B4 merely asks for a definition instead of changing the practical situation.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 identifies the withheld code but does not deepen A's control beyond A3.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1's unspecified proposal gives little setting, and B2's funding code supplies the first concrete mechanism.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Six digits' neatly answers B4, though the exchange functions partly as an explanation of the card.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"The youth club trip sounds wonderful. I've helped finish the coach booking.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"Thanks. We just need your funding code.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Of course. I'll send it when I'm comfortable releasing it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I'll sit with you while you check the figures.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"How kind. The figures are fine. You can help me write a reassuring update while everyone waits.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A supplies practical help and reassurance while withholding the personal consent required to release funding.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Administrative caution about incorrect figures.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5 explicitly accepts the figures as correct but keeps the code withheld, revealing that A3's private comfort remains decisive.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b makes a helpful colleague's checking offer become assistance with managing the delay; a follows an organizer trying another venue.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original B4–A5 explained the premise without changing action. The new illustrative setting is a youth club coach booking. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. B4 offers to resolve uncertainty; A5 accepts the help for reassurance while preserving the private veto. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The comedy is restrained and depends on the gap between A's helpful tone and continued withholding.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S55-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d00ca72980251c5f6829400a248c5e82d9ccdfe785d7633ead06e4ed4ee40049\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 invokes the shared packing line and A3 erases the title; A5 shifts toward B's greater purchasing power.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 specifically answers B2's title request; A5 interprets B4's changed circumstances as ability to afford biscuits.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 wants workplace formality from an old colleague and B4 insists their present positions differ.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 upgrades biscuit price but does not intensify the shared-beginnings argument.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes former biscuit packers sharing biscuits with one