\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 preserves competitive evidence even when the meeting that would justify it no longer exists.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 names Sam and a missed meeting; A5 keeps the attendance record as the concrete recurring object.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's 'comfortably ahead' and A5's attendance claim compactly maintain the imaginary contest.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Sam's missed the stock meeting. Another point to me for next manager.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"He's unloading the delivery. Cancel the meeting and help him.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"I'll record my attendance, then my flexibility.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"Sam asked for you specifically. He says you're good at stacking.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Put that under endorsements. I'll stack beside him so we can see whose pile stays up.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A interprets absence, useful work and a colleague's compliment as comparative evidence in a continuing contest to become manager.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General conscientiousness or recordkeeping.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 explicitly awards a leadership point; A3 preserves credit after B2 corrects the absence, and A5 converts B4's stacking compliment into endorsement and direct comparison.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a assigns unequal roles to make a shared repair demonstrate leadership; b treats a rival's request for help as endorsement, then creates a side-by-side comparison. The frozen a record retains its earlier comparison as required.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The rejected candidate gave B no reason to cancel and ended by repeating attendance bookkeeping. The revision keeps Sam, a missed meeting and cancellation, adding a delivery that explains both absence and B's practical request. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, because A1/A3/A5 turn each new fact into leadership evidence; logic 5, because B2's work request produces flexibility credit and B4's specific compliment produces endorsement and stacking competition; relationship 4, because B needs the delivery unloaded and supplies Sam's cooperative request; heightening 4, because A5 moves from recording attendance to testing performance against Sam; specificity 5, because A1's stock meeting and B2/B4's delivery and stacking establish immediate work; brevity/wit 4, because A5's endorsement category follows the compliment before the physical comparison. Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; all dialogue gates pass. Original firstPass remains unchanged.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Both alternatives now involve practical cooperation, but their tactics differ: a reserves the leadership role, while b competes at the same task after appropriating praise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S59-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ff7f77da753dd7f3f43f5963fce5e5c4d9a0fded6a0c4870c666a7be467b3ff7\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 requests judgment while calling it a formality; A3 asks for more under the label of confirming A's suspicion.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 appropriates B2's criticism as prior suspicion; A5 uses that framing to reject B4's credit request.\"\n          },\n          \"rela