ng.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a minimizes authorship and editorial credit in a wedding speech; b minimizes a navigator's influence while continuing to request route decisions.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original final beat denied influence without renewing reliance. The new illustrative setting is a wedding speech with a specific unsuitable joke. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity/wit 4 = 92. B4 offers a credited story; A5 reduces the credit while revealing dependence on its missing ending. Five spoken ABABA turns; under 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The recently separated parents provide stakes, not the joke's target; the comic focus is A's refusal to acknowledge B.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S59-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a500e30ca190972affbe305ac8c5a703be96817bff6adaa12747f864b2f8dd96\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 asks for advice and A3 claims it was a test, but A5 only protects face rather than continuing to use B's judgment.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 incorporates B2's bridge closure as supposed test knowledge; A5 answers B4's westward-heading correction with an inspection excuse.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 gives useful navigation information and B4 catches A's inconsistency, but B's continuing role remains thin.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 makes the denial more elaborate without increasing A's dependence on B.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2's east road and closed west bridge provide concrete directions that remain coherent t